\ Exp 034: Execute, alias, constant (Forth-level), bracket state

\ execute — call the xt on TOS
\ Pushes xt to return stack, then returns — which jumps to xt
: execute >r ;

\ :.` — continuation entry point (alias for :`)
: :.` :` ;

\ _alias — set xt of most recent header, mark as alias, start anon
\ ( xt -- ) stores xt into header, sets $20 flag, opens new anon
: _alias H@ ! $20 H@ ct|! anon:` ;

\ alias` — create a named synonym
\ Usage: value-on-stack alias name
\ :` calls _colon which calls _semi_exec, executing pending anon code
\ that puts the xt on the stack. Then _alias stores it in the new header.
: alias` :` _alias ;

\ Forth-level constant` — alternative to assembly constant
\ :` creates header, then we set ct=1 and store value as xt
: constant` :` 1 H@ ct|! H@ ! anon:` ;

\ myconst — wrapper to test the Forth constant` without shell backtick issues
\ When user types "99 myconst val", backtick mangling finds myconst`,
\ which calls constant` to create val with value 99
: myconst` constant` ;

\ [` — suspend current definition, start new anonymous def
\ Saves current anon pointer and SC state, resets for new anon
: [` anon@ SC c@ anon:` ;

\ ]` — complete and execute current anonymous def, restore prior state
\ ;` calls _semi to end the anonymous def (execute it)
\ Then restores saved SC and anon values
: ]` 2>r ;` 2r> SC c! anon ! ;
